        <body>
            <div xml:id="d131">

                <pb facs="0299" n="199" sameAs="frus:frus1884/pg199"/>

                <head>No. 131.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Davis to Mr. Kasson.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1884-08-22"><hi rendition="#italic">August</hi> 22,
                        1884</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 5.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I inclose herewith, for your information,
                    copies of letters to this Department from Mr. Charles Weniger, a naturalized
                    American citizen residing in the city of New York, who alleges that the German
                    authorities are about to seize his inheritance in the city of Königsee, to
                    enforce the payment of a fine assessed against him for the non performance of
                    military service in Germany.</p>
                <p>I will thank you to investigate the matter, and to take such action as the facts
                    may be found to warrant.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>JOHN DAVIS,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Acting
                        Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>




                <xi:include href="d131-a1.xml" xpointer="d131-a1"/>
